      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree aea323b50b9681f546ff60f37d3baea7822c690a\nparent 107ecee166a4ddf7acb8d9cc9b8627888becea91\nauthor Hennadii Stepanov <32963518+hebasto@users.noreply.github.com> 1794657882 +0000\ncommitter fanquake <fanquake@gmail.com> 1794931870 +0000\n\nmemusage: Make fields of STL helper structs public\n\nThe `stl_tree_node`, `list_node` and `unordered_node` class templates\nonly mimic the layout of the standard library's container nodes, so\nthat `sizeof` yields an estimate of the memory they use. Their fields\nare never accessed.\n\nSince llvm/llvm-project#237374, Clang 24 diagnoses these fields with\n`-Wunused-private-field`.\n\nThis change drops the `private:` access specifiers. It does not affect\nthe size or alignment of the structs, as all their fields keep the same\naccess control, and it is consistent with `stl_shared_counter`.\n\nGithub-Pull: #36869\nRebased-From: b9a6b0ca51801e95956b7d5307d5b198b9fb7d3f\n",
